  "helpBloom": "Cognitive Level (Bloom) measures the depth of thinking on six levels:\n\n1. Remembering (0.5)\n2. Understanding (1.5)\n3. Applying (2.5)\n4. Analyzing (3.5)\n5. Evaluating (4.5)\n6. Creating (5.5)\n\nStrategic Depth describes how complex mental models you use in problem solving.",
  "helpToulmin": "The Toulmin model evaluates the structural integrity of an argument:\n\n• Claim: What is being asserted?\n• Warrant: Why is the claim true?\n• Backing: Evidence supporting the warrant.\n\nScoring (0-6) is based on the presence and quality of these elements.",
  "helpWalton": "The Walton scheme identifies the reasoning pattern used (e.g. 'Inference to the Best Explanation') and challenges it with critical questions. It does not give points, but ensures logic quality by challenging its weaknesses.",
  "helpControlRatio": "NOTE: Role and Control Ratio are distinct metrics.\n\n• **Role** is the AI's qualitative assessment of your interaction.\n• **Control Ratio** is a mathematical metric (commands / turns).\n\nDiscrepancies (e.g. Driver 0%) arise from different analysis methods. Trust the Role primarily.\n\nReference intervals:\n• < 50%: Passenger\n• 50-80%: Navigator\n• 80-150%: Driver\n• > 150%: Architect",
  "helpMethodology": "The Methodological Log tells what analysis methods the AI has applied in this phase (e.g. 'Logic Audit', 'Causality Testing').",
